+- **`trim` action**: Removes leading and trailing whitespace (including
+  newlines) from `source_labels` joined with `separator`, and writes the
+  result to `target_label`. This is useful for cleaning up label values that
+  picked up stray whitespace, e.g. from a scraped source or from concatenating
+  several label values together. Example: strip whitespace from the `foo`
+  label value:
+
+  ```yaml {hl_lines=[1]}
+  - action: trim
+    source_labels: ["foo"]
+    target_label: "foo"
+  ```
+
+  [Try the above config](https://play.victoriametrics.com/select/0/prometheus/graph/#/relabeling?config=-+action%3A+trim%0A++source_labels%3A+%5B%22foo%22%5D%0A++target_label%3A+%22foo%22&labels=%7B__name__%3D%22node_cpu_seconds_total%22%2C+foo%3D%22%20bar%5Cn%22%7D)
+
